{
 "title": "Act 1: Six Flags",
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "Act 1: Six Flags",
   "beats": [
    {
     "id": "a1_intro",
     "shot": "a1_intro",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "To understand Tuesday, you have to understand one thing."
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_hands",
     "shot": "a1_hands",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Texas has changed hands more than almost any place in America, and"
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_behind",
     "shot": "a1_behind",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "every handover left something behind that still shapes how Texans vote."
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_flags",
     "shot": "a1_flags",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Six different *flags* have flown over it.",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pops",
       "w:flags",
       0.6
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_native",
     "shot": "a1_native",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Long before any of them, this land belonged to dozens of *Native* nations.",
     "date": 1500
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_caddo",
     "shot": "a1_caddo",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "The *Caddo* farmed the east."
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_karank",
     "shot": "a1_karank",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "The *Karankawa* fished the coast.",
     "amb": "waves"
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_comanche",
     "shot": "a1_comanche",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "And on the plains, the *Comanche* built one of the most powerful horse empires in North America.",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "gallop",
       "w:Comanche",
       0.5
      ]
     ],
     "amb": "wind"
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_spain",
     "shot": "a1_spain",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Flag number one, *Spain*.",
     "date": 1718
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_mission",
     "shot": "a1_mission",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "In 1718, Spanish missionaries founded a mission beside the San Antonio River."
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_alamo",
     "shot": "a1_alamo",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "You know it by a different name, *the Alamo*.",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "ding",
       "w:Alamo",
       0.6
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_france",
     "shot": "a1_france",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Flag number two, *France*.",
     "date": 1685
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_lasalle",
     "shot": "a1_lasalle",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "For a few years in the 1680s, a French explorer named La Salle planted",
     "amb": "waves"
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_fort",
     "shot": "a1_fort",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "a little fort on the Texas coast.",
     "amb": "waves"
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_badly",
     "shot": "a1_badly",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "It did *not* go well.",
     "gag": true
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_wiped",
     "shot": "a1_wiped",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Disease, hunger, and attacks wiped it out.",
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_held",
     "shot": "a1_held",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Spain held on 100 years, but it never really filled the place.",
     "date": 1800
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_few",
     "shot": "a1_few",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "By the early 1800s, Spanish Texas had only a few *thousand* settlers."
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_border",
     "shot": "a1_border",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Hold on to that empty border."
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_fills",
     "shot": "a1_fills",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "In Texas, whoever *fills* the land ends up running it, and that is still true in 2026."
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_mexico",
     "shot": "a1_mexico",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Flag number three, *Mexico*.",
     "date": 1821
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_indep",
     "shot": "a1_indep",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "In 1821, Mexico won its independence from Spain and inherited a giant empty Texas."
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_risky",
     "shot": "a1_risky",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "So Mexico tried something *risky*."
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_invite",
     "shot": "a1_invite",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "It invited *Americans* in.",
     "gag": true,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "boing",
       "w:Americans",
       0.6
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_austin",
     "shot": "a1_austin",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "A man named Stephen F. Austin brought the first 300 families."
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_cheap",
     "shot": "a1_cheap",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Land was *cheap*.",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "kaching",
       "w:cheap",
       0.6
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_slaves",
     "shot": "a1_slaves",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Tens of thousands followed, and many of them brought something Mexico was moving to ban, enslaved people.",
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_abol",
     "shot": "a1_abol",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Mexico abolished slavery in 1829.",
     "date": 1829,
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_loop",
     "shot": "a1_loop",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Texas settlers looked for loopholes, labeling enslaved workers as indentured servants.",
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_ten",
     "shot": "a1_ten",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "By the 1830s, Americans in Texas outnumbered Mexicans by about *ten* to one.",
     "date": 1834
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_grip",
     "shot": "a1_grip",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Mexico tightened its grip."
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_push",
     "shot": "a1_push",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Texans pushed back."
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_first",
     "shot": "a1_first",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "It was the first time newcomers changed who ran Texas."
    },
    {
     "id": "a1_last",
     "shot": "a1_last",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "It would not be the *last*."
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}